e-asset-provisioning walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the Aster Diagnostics provisioning workflow + inventory audit,
authored and self-reviewed in-session.

Scope: fictional Aster Diagnostics (continued); gates: purchase, cloud creation,
onboarding, software install, data acquisition. All company facts fictional.
Artifacts authored:
  - Provisioning workflow, 7 steps: request -> approval (tier recorded) -> secure
    build -> CMDB record before deploy -> deploy+verify -> change-driven updates ->
    deprovision (sanitize, mark retired w/ history, revoke, release)
  - CMDB record definition tested against CM-8 (accurate, complete, no duplicates,
    right granularity, accountability info)
  - Inventory audit: discovery (network + cloud enumeration) reconciled vs CMDB;
    purchases vs deployments; owners vs HR roster. 5 findings, each with decision /
    owner / date:
    1. 23 shadow cloud instances -> 17 retro-provisioned, 6 shut down
    2. 31 assets owned by departed staff -> transfer in 2 weeks; HR-feed trigger
    3. ghost lab server w/ Confidential data, never ticketed -> sanitized per
       800-88r2, retired properly; retirement-ticket requirement added
    4. 14 duplicate laptop records (CMDB + spreadsheet) -> spreadsheet retired as
       system of record; CMDB authoritative; duplicates merged
    5. 9 unverified builds -> verified retroactively (2 remediated); verification
       made a merge-gate
  - Audit close-out: next audit scheduled (quarterly discovery, annual full)

